<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Norodom Sihamoni</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1953">1953</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Norodom Sihamoni has been king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a> since 2004, chosen by the Throne Council after his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-sihanouk">Norodom Sihanouk</a> abdicated. Before his accession he was a ballet dancer and teacher in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> and Cambodia's ambassador to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco">UNESCO</a>. As constitutional monarch he has limited powers, while real authority has rested with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hun-sen">Hun Sen</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodian-peoples-party">Cambodian People's Party</a>.</p></div>
